AB  - The concept of entrainment was originally a biological response in an organism to a stream of stimuli in which the organism in some way shows a resonant response in frequency to the stimuli. Audio-Visual Entrainment (AVE) involves the presentation of a continuous stream of visual flashes of light and auditory pulses of tones. This is purported to induce a brainwave frequency response, matching that of the stimuli, also known as the frequency following response and more recently referred to as brainwave entrainment. The frequency following (entrainment) response is only a small portion of what AVE does and sometimes it doesn’t occur at all. Additional effects of AVE include dissociation and hypnotic induction; autonomic nervous system calming; increased cerebral blood flow; increases in beneficial neurotransmitters, and boosted lactate/ATP, heat shock protein-70 and glia function. Through these mechanisms of action, AVE can quickly calm and “re-boot” the brain, thus restoring cognition, emotion control and affect. AVE and its variants (Randomized AVE or RAVE, which employs both entraining and mildly random stimulation and Audio-visual Stimulation (AVS), which is often randomized to the point of having no entrainment value at all, are the most fascinating of stimulation technologies because of the many effects they have on the whole brain and mind.
